    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d705">

                <pb facs="0745" n="487" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg487"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 300.115/4359</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at London</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Skinner</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-07-27">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 27, 1915</hi>.</date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 3 p. m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Relative to <hi rendition="#italic">Ogeechee</hi>, officially informed that
                    Holman Gregory, on behalf Crown, will sit at Treasury from and after August 2
                    to, meet representatives cargo interests. Am unofficially advised if this
                    referee satisfied that transactions were <hi rendition="#italic">bona fide</hi>
                    and entered into before issue order March 11, he will report in favor of
                        release.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d705-f1"/> Am pressing for extension this plan
                    to cargo <hi rendition="#italic">F. J. Lisman, Seaconnet</hi> and other
                    similarly situated ships.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Skinner</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d705-f1" n="1" xml:id="d705-f1-content">
                <p>A second circular, containing this information, was sent out by the Department to
                    the shippers, and releases in practically all cases were subsequently
                    secured.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
